module DASHI.Moonshine.OggSSP4A2BIntegralRestrictionRefinementExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 4A -> 2B INTEGRAL RESTRICTION REFINEMENT
--
-- EXTERNAL SOURCES
--
-- ATLAS of Finite Group Representations:
--   the Monster power map records 4A under the power-up column of 2B.
--   Equivalently, for g in class 4A, g^2 lies in class 2B.
--
-- Carnahan--Urano, "Monstrous Moonshine for Integral Group Rings":
--   for cyclic subgroups generated by a 4A element, the integral Moonshine
--   module is explicitly decomposed into indecomposable integral group-ring
--   modules and the multiplicities are determined.
--
-- DASHI CONTRIBUTION
--
-- Formalize the exact square-subgroup inclusion
--
--     C2 = <g^2>  -->  C4 = <g>
--
-- and the resulting restriction of any invertible C4 action to C2.
--
-- This gives a canonical SOURCE-NATIVE refinement lane for 2B: one may retain
-- the finer 4A/C4 indecomposable label before forgetting to the square-subgroup
-- 2B action.
--
-- ATTRIBUTION FIREWALL
--
-- Neither ATLAS nor Carnahan--Urano identifies the restricted 4A
-- indecomposable labels with the five characteristic-2 inertia sectors.
-- Neither source proves the 3,3,2,1,1 localized DVR-length law.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

